sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Frontend
    participant API as FastAPI Route
    participant AuthService
    participant UserRepo as UserRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant OTPService
    participant Redis
    participant EmailService
    participant SMTP

    User->>+Frontend: Click "Forgot Password"<br/>Enter email
    Frontend->>+API: POST /auth/forgot-password<br/>{email}
    
    API->>+AuthService: request_password_reset(email)
    
    rect rgb(230, 240, 255)
        Note over AuthService,DB: Step 1: Validate User
        AuthService->>+UserRepo: get_user_by_email(email)
        UserRepo->>+DB: SELECT * FROM users<br/>WHERE email = ?
        DB-->>-UserRepo: User or None
        UserRepo-->>-AuthService: UserDTO or None
        
        alt User not found
            Note over AuthService: Security: Don't reveal<br/>if email exists
            AuthService-->>API: {message: "If email exists,<br/>OTP sent"}
            API-->>Frontend: 200 OK
            Frontend-->>User: Check your email for OTP
        end
        
        alt User not verified
            AuthService-->>API: HTTPException(400,<br/>"Verify email first")
            API-->>Frontend: 400 Bad Request
            Frontend-->>User: Please verify your email first
        end
    end
    
    rect rgb(255, 240, 230)
        Note over AuthService,SMTP: Step 2: Generate & Send OTP
        AuthService->>+OTPService: generate_otp(user_id, email)
        
        OTPService->>OTPService: Generate 6-digit OTP<br/>(random.randint(100000, 999999))
        
        OTPService->>+Redis: Check existing attempts:<br/>GET reset_attempts:{user_id}
        Redis-->>-OTPService: Attempt count or None
        
        alt Exceeded rate limit (3 attempts)
            OTPService-->>AuthService: HTTPException(429,<br/>"Too many attempts")
            AuthService-->>API: 429 Too Many Requests
            API-->>Frontend: Error
            Frontend-->>User: Too many attempts,<br/>wait 5 minutes
        end
        
        OTPService->>+Redis: SET reset_otp:{user_id} = {otp}<br/>EX 300 (5 minutes)
        Redis-->>-OTPService: OTP stored
        
        OTPService->>+Redis: INCR reset_attempts:{user_id}<br/>EX 300 (5 minutes)
        Redis-->>-OTPService: Attempt count incremented
        
        OTPService->>+EmailService: send_otp_email(email, otp)
        EmailService->>EmailService: Build email:<br/>"Your OTP: {otp}<br/>Valid for 5 minutes"
        
        EmailService->>+SMTP: Send email via SMTP
        SMTP-->>-EmailService: Email sent
        EmailService-->>-OTPService: OTP email sent
        
        OTPService-->>-AuthService: OTP generated and sent
        AuthService-->>-API: {message: "OTP sent to email"}
    end
    
    API-->>-Frontend: 200 OK
    Frontend-->>-User: Check your email<br/>for 6-digit OTP
    
    Note over User: User receives email<br/>with OTP code
